WEBVTT

00:00:05.239 --> 00:00:06.240
Oh!

00:00:07.199 --> 00:00:09.326
Whoo-hoo!

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.619
JULIAN: Yeah!

00:00:10.703 --> 00:00:12.955
Catching mad air on the half-pipe!

00:00:13.038 --> 00:00:14.415
This is crazy.

00:00:14.498 --> 00:00:17.668
Do you think they know
they are living in a magnetic bull's-eye?

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:20.754
Doesn't look like a lot of
doomsday prepping going on in here.

00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:22.131
BROOKE: I can't believe it!

00:00:22.214 --> 00:00:23.424
Visitors!

00:00:23.507 --> 00:00:26.093
We've never had visitors. (chuckles)

00:00:26.176 --> 00:00:28.971
Somebody pinch me. Or should I pinch you?

00:00:29.054 --> 00:00:31.473
-Wait, I'll pinch both of us.
-(both chuckling)

00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:34.268
Did I hit my head? What's happening here?

00:00:35.102 --> 00:00:37.062
I sure hope this isn't a... Oh!

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.691
Dream!

00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:44.987
♪ Dream Weaver ♪

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.198
♪ I believe you can get me through the night ♪

00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:49.283
(whistles)

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.951
(whinnying)

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:54.371
This guy? For real?

00:00:54.455 --> 00:00:56.290
-Whatever.
-(yelps)

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.625
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:01.336
Hello, handsome.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.796
I'm Brooke.

00:01:03.297 --> 00:01:04.715
(chuckling)

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:07.134
Ooh. Such exquisite bone structure.

00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:09.053
Such a strong jaw.

00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:11.513
I'm getting butterflies!

00:01:11.597 --> 00:01:13.307
I'm getting nauseous.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.225
Sorry to interrupt this
weirdo love connection

00:01:15.309 --> 00:01:16.894
but we're kind of in a hurry.

00:01:16.977 --> 00:01:18.395
If we don't do something fast,

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:21.607
that asteroid is gonna
blow us all to smithereens.

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:25.069
Oh. That sounds urgent.

00:01:25.152 --> 00:01:26.862
I better take you to him.

00:01:26.945 --> 00:01:28.989
Who's "him"? Your leader?

00:01:29.073 --> 00:01:31.742
He is our everything.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.243
BOTH: He sees all.

00:01:33.327 --> 00:01:34.661
He knows all.

00:01:34.745 --> 00:01:37.331
And smells amazing!

00:01:37.915 --> 00:01:40.209
Okay. Okay. He sounds great. Let's go!

00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:42.252
Brilliant. Right this way.

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:44.338
(Sid screaming)

00:01:46.423 --> 00:01:48.759
(all screaming)

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.927
BUCK: (laughing) Whoo-hoo!

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.011
Yes!

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.098
(Manny yelping)

00:01:54.181 --> 00:01:56.183
BROOKE: Please keep your arms and legs

00:01:56.266 --> 00:01:58.769
inside the tram at all times.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:02.189
But allow your spirit to roam free

00:02:02.272 --> 00:02:04.608
in Geotopia.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.693
I have a good feeling about this.

00:02:06.777 --> 00:02:08.278
Maybe he'll be able to help us.

00:02:08.362 --> 00:02:10.030
She did say he knows all.

00:02:10.114 --> 00:02:11.782
And all's a lot!

00:02:16.161 --> 00:02:17.621
Here he is.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:21.583
The Master of Meditation,
the Supreme Serene,

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:25.379
the four-time Heavy Thoughts
champion of the world!

00:02:25.963 --> 00:02:27.172
(bangs gong)

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.641
(spits)

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.477
Is that a llama? I hate llamas.

00:02:40.561 --> 00:02:42.312
They spit and smell.

00:02:42.396 --> 00:02:43.480
So does she.

00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:45.232
BOTH: So do we! (laughing)

00:02:52.531 --> 00:02:55.075
Oh! (laughing)

00:02:55.159 --> 00:02:56.660
Greetings, mammals!

00:02:56.743 --> 00:03:00.747
The Shangri Llama will see you...

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.126
Now.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:05.252
Ooh. Wonderful.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:07.838
So where is he?

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.007
He is here. Talking to you.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.968
Oh, I get it. He's a ventriloquist

00:03:13.051 --> 00:03:14.261
and you're the dummy.

00:03:14.595 --> 00:03:16.471
-No, you're the dummy.
-No, you're the dummy.

00:03:16.555 --> 00:03:17.514
No, you're the dummy.

00:03:17.598 --> 00:03:18.974
This is the guy that's going to save us.

00:03:19.057 --> 00:03:20.350
Look within. You're the dummy. (spits)

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.768
(gasps)

00:03:21.852 --> 00:03:23.937
Disgusting! Loved that!

00:03:24.021 --> 00:03:26.690
New topic. We're all about to die.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.776
Well, that's no good. Stress is a killer.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.529
Let us loosen our limbs and open our minds.

00:03:32.613 --> 00:03:33.947
Downward Dog!

00:03:34.907 --> 00:03:36.325
Uh... Seriously?

00:03:36.408 --> 00:03:39.620
I'll wait. I have all the time in the world.

00:03:39.703 --> 00:03:40.704
(groaning)

00:03:41.622 --> 00:03:42.789
(grunts)

00:03:43.207 --> 00:03:44.875
Actually, you don't have
all the time in the world.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:48.670
None of us do. You see,
there's this thing in the sky.

00:03:48.754 --> 00:03:52.049
Oh. That blinding light
that seems to get larger by the minute?

00:03:52.132 --> 00:03:54.218
(laughs) What about it? Seems fine to me.

00:03:54.927 --> 00:03:56.845
With all due respect, Your Twistiness,

00:03:56.929 --> 00:03:58.180
that's an asteroid.

00:03:58.263 --> 00:04:00.182
It's magnetically attracted to this place

00:04:00.265 --> 00:04:02.059
and it's heading straight for us.

00:04:02.142 --> 00:04:03.977
(spits) Aha!

00:04:04.061 --> 00:04:06.396
It must desire our magnetic crystals.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.731
Well, who can blame it?

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.358
They're really quite something.

00:04:09.441 --> 00:04:11.693
Did you know their power
grants eternal youth?

00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:14.238
I am over 400 years old. Mmm-hmm.

00:04:14.321 --> 00:04:16.031
-That's not possible.
-TEDDY: Sure it is.

00:04:16.114 --> 00:04:18.909
I'm 326! Whoo!

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:21.828
Huh? You don't look a day over 275.

00:04:22.412 --> 00:04:25.707
We are young, happy and safe.
And we always will be.

00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:28.585
(echoing) Thanks to Geotopia!

00:04:28.669 --> 00:04:30.420
Kudos. It is lovely.

00:04:30.504 --> 00:04:33.257
Now, let's figure out
a way to launch it into space!

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.592
I'm sorry. You want to destroy our home?

00:04:35.676 --> 00:04:37.552
It'll be destroyed either way.

00:04:37.636 --> 00:04:41.098
But if we propel this magnetic material
into the atmosphere,

00:04:41.181 --> 00:04:44.059
we can change the asteroid's path
and save everyone.

00:04:44.142 --> 00:04:45.519
What do you say?

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.020
Caterpillar!

00:04:48.605 --> 00:04:51.441
So, is that a yes? Or... (gasps)

00:04:51.525 --> 00:04:52.567
-(groaning)
-Oh.

00:04:52.651 --> 00:04:56.321
You are storing a lot of hostility
in your lower spine.

00:04:57.155 --> 00:04:58.448
Shangri Llama, how are we gonna...

00:04:58.532 --> 00:05:01.243
Funky Chicken. Jiggy Jelly. Mashed Potato.

00:05:01.326 --> 00:05:03.704
Your flexibility is a sight to behold.

00:05:03.787 --> 00:05:06.540
Now how the devil
are we going to launch these crystals?

00:05:06.623 --> 00:05:08.375
You can't. It's impossible.

00:05:09.126 --> 00:05:10.961
Whoo! I am bushed.

00:05:12.796 --> 00:05:14.131
Awesome meeting you guys.

00:05:14.214 --> 00:05:16.550
Feel free to hang or, you know, whatever.

00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:17.634
(spits)

00:05:18.218 --> 00:05:19.261
Hmm.

00:05:19.344 --> 00:05:22.097
That's it. He was our last hope.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.390
We're doomed.

00:05:23.473 --> 00:05:25.809
Yeah. All we got was a free yoga class.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:28.478
(grunting) On that subject,

00:05:28.562 --> 00:05:30.147
could you help me, please?

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.066
My nose is dangerously close to my butt.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.902
Uh, Sid, why do you have two tails?

00:05:35.986 --> 00:05:37.654
GRANNY: I'm in here, too.

00:05:37.738 --> 00:05:38.905
(chuckling nervously)

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.954
-(Peaches crying)
-Hey, don't cry.

00:05:46.038 --> 00:05:47.497
Look on the bright side.

00:05:47.831 --> 00:05:50.917
We get to see our lives
flash before our eyes.

00:05:51.585 --> 00:05:55.172
That means I get to fall in love with you

00:05:55.255 --> 00:05:56.673
all over again.

00:05:56.757 --> 00:05:57.841
(chuckles)

00:05:57.924 --> 00:06:01.595
Only you can make the end of the world
sound like a good thing.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.102
We did a good job raising her.

00:06:09.186 --> 00:06:10.854
She's stronger than we know.

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:14.524
Two days ago, I'd have given
anything to keep her with us.

00:06:14.608 --> 00:06:17.778
Now I'd give anything
just to see her get married,

00:06:17.861 --> 00:06:19.446
and leave home.

00:06:19.529 --> 00:06:22.491
Play with her kids, dance with her husband.

00:06:22.574 --> 00:06:24.868
Yell at him when
he forgets their anniversary.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:25.952
(chuckles)

00:06:27.537 --> 00:06:29.081
ELLIE: It was a good one, wasn't it?

00:06:29.748 --> 00:06:32.834
Our life? You, me, and Peaches.

00:06:32.918 --> 00:06:34.294
The best.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.049
(playing soft music)

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:40.884
SID: Oh, Brooke.

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.552
You're so pretty.

00:06:42.636 --> 00:06:44.930
You take my lisp away.

00:06:45.472 --> 00:06:48.016
(chuckles) I bet you say that
to all the girls.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.061
I try. But usually they run away too fast.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.354
(chuckles)

00:06:52.437 --> 00:06:54.648
Oh, you're such a romantic.

00:06:55.399 --> 00:06:58.235
Hey, I know this is going to
sound super forward

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.738
but will you be my mate for life?

00:07:01.822 --> 00:07:04.491
Oh, Brooke, I don't know what to say.

00:07:04.574 --> 00:07:06.576
It's only been twelve minutes.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.412
What took you so long?

00:07:08.495 --> 00:07:12.666
Yes! This has been
the best last day on Earth ever.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:14.751
(gasps) A diamond! I need a diamond!

00:07:14.835 --> 00:07:16.086
Where can I find a...

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:18.046
Oh! Perfect.

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.172
(straining)

00:07:19.256 --> 00:07:21.925
No, no, no. Sid, sweetie, don't do that.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:27.681
Nonsense. Only the best
for my one... true... love.

00:07:28.974 --> 00:07:29.975
(groans)

00:07:31.435 --> 00:07:32.436
(gasps)

00:07:32.811 --> 00:07:34.020
(crystals clinking)

